Rationale: layered tokens enable visual change without changing component intent.
Naming: lowercase dot notation; semantic names describe purpose, not hue or location.
Coverage: color, typography, spacing, radius, border, elevation, motion, focus, and density.
Quality gate: every component token maps to a semantic token, every semantic token maps to a foundation value, and contrast and focus values are verified.
Repository path intent: /projects/project-001/design/sections/g/token-map.mmd.
Writing rule: use sentence case, concise labels, action-first controls, and no decorative copy.
Publishing rule: version changes, preserve migration aliases, and record removals in the audit record.